# FR-402 band-gated reactions for Dom.
#
# Each title below is the WARM route for one NPC that `canon/dom/characters`
# already declares `"involvement": "reputation_reaction"`, with a hook_summary
# naming the faction and the band. `globals/npc_reactions.gd` attaches them;
# `dialogue/dom_townsfolk.dialogue` stays the generated neutral fallback and is
# never hand-edited (tools/generate_gloot.gd owns it).

~ dom_raika_toll_warm
Raika Toll: Keep your footing. The stones are honest. The rest of the Arm is not.
Raika Toll: The Sentinels have you written down as someone who brings back a true count. That buys one entry out of the Wound-Watch ledger. One.
- "Read me the entry."
	Raika Toll: Fourteenth of the tolling month. A wall-hand went out past the Lip on a listed patrol and came back on nobody's list at all.
	Raika Toll: The line beneath it says CLOSED, NO FAULT. It is written in a different hand than the rest of the page.
	Raika Toll: I have not asked whose hand. You may. Do it somewhere the bell cannot hear you.
	=> END
- "Keep it. I would rather owe you."
	Raika Toll: Sensible. An entry spends once. A toll keeper who likes you spends for years.
	=> END

~ dom_edda_broadmark_warm
Edda Broadmark: The Companies give your name weight. Edda does the same, and Edda is the harder of the two to move.
Edda Broadmark: I have a veteran off the muster rolls. Two good knees and no war left in her. She will walk a road with you and not ask which road.
- "Send her."
	Edda Broadmark: Then she is sent. She answers to Broadmark, and Broadmark answers to whoever brings her back breathing.
	=> END
- "Not yet. I would only get her killed."
	Edda Broadmark: Honest. Rare. The offer keeps — it is in the book, and the book outlives the both of us.
	=> END

~ dom_drann_wetiron_warm
Drann Wetiron: Mind the sparks. The Concord speaks your name warmly, which obliges me to be civil in front of the apprentices.
Drann Wetiron: The honest forge is the second one, behind the slack tub. It is yours between hammer falls. Do not make me regret the civility.
=> END

~ dom_venn_ashcord_warm
Venn Ashcord: I waive no line. Everyone queues. But a warm record decides which drawer I open first, and today it is the useful one.
Venn Ashcord: Fourth cabinet, the drawer the damp got into. Half of what Dom would rather forget is in there, and all of it is filed under WEATHER.
=> END

~ dom_holst_brinevein_warm
Holst Brinevein: The Menders vouch for you, and the Menders are stingy with vouching.
Holst Brinevein: So. The sea-mouth. Keep the broken tower off your right shoulder until the water goes the colour of old tin, then cut hard for the Lip.
Holst Brinevein: The straight line is faster. The straight line is also where we stopped counting.
=> END
